<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n943" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγρό-τερος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγρός</span>; properly opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρέσ-τερος</span>) poet. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄγριος</span>, in <i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i> always of <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>wild</i>
			animals, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμίονοι, σύες, αἶγες</span>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.852
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				12.146
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				17.295
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγροτέρης ἐλάφοιο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Sc.</u>
					407
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φὴρ ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					3.4
				</span></i>
			: abs., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγρότεροι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					8.58
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. καὶ νέποδες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					6.11
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Satyr.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of
				<i>countrymen,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				AP
				9.244
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Apollonid.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>APl.</u>
				4.235
			</span></i> (Id.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> of
			plants, <i>wild,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				AP
				9.384.8
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				711
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Coluth.
				111
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄγρα</span>) <i>fond of the chase,
			huntress</i>, of the nymph Cyrene, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				9.6
			</span></i>: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέριμνα ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>O.</u>
					2.60
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> pr. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀγροτέρα</span>, Artemis <i>the
			huntress</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				21.471
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyn.</u>
				6.13
			</span></i>; worshipped at Agra in Attica, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				2.467
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				1.19.6
			</span></i>; at Sparta and elsewhere, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				4.2.20
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				660
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
